# SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0
#
# Declarative competency questions for the GTS transport slice, authored as
# slice-resident test-DSL data and executed by the native Rust slice-test harness
# (crates/slicetest) over the full merged ontology, asserted lane
# (gmeow:reasoningNone is the default).
#
# The questions below are the MEDIUM AXIS's own acceptance surface: a medium is a
# lawful (encode, decode) pair, a dictionary is a byte table trained over declared
# material, and an envelope is the RDF projection of what a frame already carries in
# band. Each of those claims is only as good as the graph's ability to ANSWER it, so
# every question here is one a consumer, a reviewer, or the build itself must be able
# to put to the graph before it decodes, ships, or grades anything.
#
# Every expected row is a real result of the bound query over the merged modules —
# the row sets were read back off the harness, never enumerated by hand from prose —
# and each question declares gmeow:cqExactRows, so an unexpected EXTRA answer reds
# exactly as loudly as a missing one. That is deliberate: most of these questions are
# totality claims ("every failure class has a gate", "every reference resolves"), and
# a containment-only check cannot fail on the case that matters.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/gts/tests/> .

# =========================================================================== #
# 1. Which failure does a medium refusal raise, and which gate raises it?      #
# =========================================================================== #

ex:cqMediumFailureClasses a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQueryFile "slices/core/gts/queries/competency/medium-failure-classes.rq" ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "A refusal that cannot name its own failure class is indistinguishable from a crash, and a failure class no gate raises is a name with nothing behind it — which is exactly how a transport axis rots: the vocabulary keeps promising seven distinct refusals while the build only ever enforces four. GMEOW must therefore answer 'which named transport failure exists, and what raises it?' FROM THE GRAPH, over the gmeow:enforcesFailureClass edges themselves, so that retiring a gate or minting an unwired failure class moves this answer. If the answer is wrong the damage is silent and severe: a decoder that meets an unregistered dictionary would report the generic conformance family instead of gmeow:MediumUnknownDictionary, and an operator would look for a corrupt payload rather than a missing dictionary — the one situation in which retrying dictionary-less produces plausible garbage rather than an error." ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:shapeMediumFailureClasses ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow
        ex:rowFailureFrameProfile ,
        ex:rowFailure01 ,
        ex:rowFailure02 ,
        ex:rowFailure03 ,
        ex:rowFailure04 ,
        ex:rowFailure05 ,
        ex:rowFailure06 ,
        ex:rowFailure07 ,
        ex:rowFailure08 ,
        ex:rowFailure09 ,
        ex:rowFailure10 ,
        ex:rowFailure11 .

ex:shapeMediumFailureClasses a logic:ResultShape ;
    logic:declaresColumn
        [ logic:columnVariable "failure" ; logic:columnTermKind logic:TermKindIri ; logic:columnBinding logic:BindingRequired ] ,
        [ logic:columnVariable "gate" ; logic:columnTermKind logic:TermKindIri ; logic:columnBinding logic:BindingRequired ] ,
        [ logic:columnVariable "family" ; logic:columnTermKind logic:TermKindIri ; logic:columnBinding logic:BindingRequired ] ;
    logic:shapeCardinality logic:RowsExact .

ex:rowFailureFrameProfile a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "failure" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:GtsFrameProfileViolation ] ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "gate" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:MediumMandatedFrameProfileConstraint ] ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "family" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:GtsConformanceFailure ] .
ex:rowFailure01 a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "failure" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:MediumCorpusDrift ] ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "gate" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:MediumCorpusIdentityAgreementConstraint ] ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "family" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:GtsConformanceFailure ] .
ex:rowFailure02 a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "failure" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:MediumDictionaryRegression ] ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "gate" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:MediumDictionaryRetentionConstraint ] ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "family" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:GtsConformanceFailure ] .
ex:rowFailure03 a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "failure" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:MediumDigestMismatch ] ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "gate" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:MediumStrataDigestFormConstraint ] ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "family" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:GtsConformanceFailure ] .
ex:rowFailure04 a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "failure" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:MediumOpaqueFrame ] ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "gate" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:MediumReaderCapabilityConstraint ] ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "family" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:GtsConformanceFailure ] .
ex:rowFailure05 a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "failure" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:MediumUndeclaredDictionary ] ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "gate" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:MediumEnvelope ] ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "family" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:GtsConformanceFailure ] .
ex:rowFailure06 a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "failure" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:MediumUndeclaredDictionary ] ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "gate" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:payloadSchemaMediumRangeClosure ] ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "family" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:GtsConformanceFailure ] .
ex:rowFailure07 a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "failure" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:MediumUnknownDictionary ] ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "gate" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:envelopeDictionaryRangeClosure ] ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "family" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:GtsConformanceFailure ] .
ex:rowFailure08 a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "failure" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:MediumUnknownDictionary ] ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "gate" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:payloadSchemaDictionaryRangeClosure ] ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "family" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:GtsConformanceFailure ] .
ex:rowFailure09 a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "failure" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:MediumUnknownDictionary ] ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "gate" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:MediumDictionaryResolutionConstraint ] ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "family" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:GtsConformanceFailure ] .
ex:rowFailure10 a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "failure" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:MediumUnknownSchema ] ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "gate" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:envelopeSchemaRangeClosure ] ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "family" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:GtsConformanceFailure ] .
ex:rowFailure11 a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "failure" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:MediumUnknownSchema ] ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "gate" ; gmeow:cellValueIri logic:MediumSchemaMediumFunctionalityConstraint ] ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "family" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:GtsConformanceFailure ] .

# =========================================================================== #
# 2. What is each medium-axis record OBLIGED to carry?                        #
# =========================================================================== #

ex:cqMediumRecordContracts a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQueryFile "slices/core/gts/queries/competency/medium-record-contracts.rq" ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "The medium axis exists to remove per-call decisions, and it does that by making every record's coordinate set MANDATORY rather than customary. Reading that obligation back out of the graph — off the canonical logic: restriction axioms, which are the derive-source the SHACL surface is projected from, never off the projected shapes — is what keeps the two from drifting: a coordinate dropped from module.ttl stops being answered here even while a stale generated shape still enforces it. What breaks if the answer is wrong is specific to each record. A gmeow:MediumEnvelope short one coordinate is not a weaker projection of a frame, it is a different claim about a frame, and a reader cannot tell which. A gmeow:CompressionDictionaryRealization short its measured corpus digest cannot be checked against the committed sweep at all, so gmeow:MediumCorpusDrift becomes unraisable. A gmeow:MediumDictionaryEffectMeasurement short one operand of its two-part code leaves the pays-for-itself criterion a comparison with a missing side — no claim rather than a weak one. Note what is ABSENT and must stay absent: the authored gmeow:CompressionDictionary obliges no digest, byte length, or Dictionary_ID, because those cannot exist before the dictionary is trained and an obligation to carry them would be unsatisfiable rather than strict." ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:shapeMediumRecordContracts ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow
        ex:rowContract01 ,
        ex:rowContract02 ,
        ex:rowContract03 ,
        ex:rowContract04 ,
        ex:rowContract05 ,
        ex:rowContract06 ,
        ex:rowContract07 ,
        ex:rowContract08 ,
        ex:rowContract09 ,
        ex:rowContract10 ,
        ex:rowContract11 ,
        ex:rowContract12 ,
        ex:rowContract13 ,
        ex:rowContract14 ,
        ex:rowContract15 ,
        ex:rowContract16 ,
        ex:rowContract17 ,
        ex:rowContract18 ,
        ex:rowContract19 ,
        ex:rowContract20 ,
        ex:rowContract21 ,
        ex:rowContract22 ,
        ex:rowContract23 ,
        ex:rowContract24 ,
        ex:rowContract25 ,
        ex:rowContract26 ,
        ex:rowContract27 ,
        ex:rowContract28 ,
        ex:rowContract29 ,
        ex:rowContract30 ,
        ex:rowContract31 ,
        ex:rowContract32 ,
        ex:rowContract33 ,
        ex:rowContract34 ,
        ex:rowContract35 ,
        ex:rowContract36 ,
        ex:rowContract37 ,
        ex:rowContract38 .

