# =========================================================================== #
# 3. Which obligations are CONDITIONAL, and on what?                          #
# =========================================================================== #

ex:cqMediumGuardedObligations a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQueryFile "slices/core/gts/queries/competency/medium-guarded-obligations.rq" ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "These three are the only places in the medium axis where an obligation is guarded rather than unconditional, and each guard is load-bearing. Make the envelope's dictionary unconditionally required and gmeow:mediumProfileBaselineL12 — the explicitly dictionary-LESS medium whose whole purpose is to make the rep-to-medium assignment total — becomes inexpressible as an envelope, so 'no dictionary' would have to be modelled as an absence a frame falls into rather than a selection a producer makes. Drop the guard entirely and the opposite failure appears: a payload primed with a dictionary its frame never names is permanently undecodable while its bytes sit intact. The reader-capability guard is the same shape one level up: only a medium realized by the NON-baseline gmeow:codecZstdRsyncable must declare what it demands of a reader, and a medium that quietly raised the reader contract would let a consumer discover the gap mid-decode, which is precisely what a declared deliverable property exists to prevent. Answering this from the graph is what stops a reviewer from reading a guarded obligation as an optional one." ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:shapeMediumGuardedObligations ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow
        ex:rowGuard01 ,
        ex:rowGuard02 ,
        ex:rowGuard03 ,
        ex:rowGuardFrameProfile ,
        ex:rowGuardSealedRecipient .

ex:shapeMediumGuardedObligations a logic:ResultShape ;
    logic:declaresColumn
        [ logic:columnVariable "guarded" ; logic:columnTermKind logic:TermKindIri ; logic:columnBinding logic:BindingRequired ] ,
        [ logic:columnVariable "trigger" ; logic:columnTermKind logic:TermKindIri ; logic:columnBinding logic:BindingRequired ] ,
        [ logic:columnVariable "triggerValue" ; logic:columnTermKind logic:TermKindIri ; logic:columnBinding logic:BindingRequired ] ,
        [ logic:columnVariable "required" ; logic:columnTermKind logic:TermKindIri ; logic:columnBinding logic:BindingRequired ] ;
    logic:shapeCardinality logic:RowsExact .

